This paper establishes uniform local large-deviation asymptotics for excursions of a L\'evy process $X$ with negative drift $-\beta$ and $\alpha$-locally regularly varying L\'evy measure $\nu$, reflected at its running infimum. Under the excursion measure $\underline n$, we first prove that the lifetime $\zeta$ and height $\overline\epsilon$ satisfy \begin{equation*}
  \underline{n}\big(\zeta\in(t,t+\delta] \big) \sim \underline{n}(\overline\epsilon\in\big (\beta t,\beta t+\beta\delta]\big)
  \sim\underline{n}(\zeta)\cdot\nu\big((\beta t,\beta t+\beta \delta]\big),
  \quad \mbox{as } t\to\infty, \end{equation*} uniformly in $\delta\in[\delta_0,\infty]$ for every $\delta_0>0$. In contrast to the asymptotic equivalence of the corresponding tail events, fixed-width lifetime and height windows have asymptotically negligible relative overlap. Nevertheless, for any positive function $\theta$ satisfying $|X_t+\beta t|/\theta_t\to0$ in probability, \begin{equation*}
  \underline n\big( |\overline\epsilon-\beta t| \leq \theta_t \,\big|\, \zeta\in (t,t+\delta] \big) \sim
  \underline n\big( |\zeta-t| \leq \theta_t \,\big|\, \overline\epsilon \in (\beta t,\beta t+\beta\delta] \big) \to 1 . \end{equation*} For conditioning windows of sublinear width bounded away from zero, both conditional excursion laws converge under spatial rescaling to a single-jump process with deterministic jump size and random arrival time determined by the integrated excursion survival function. An additional time rescaling yields the same deterministic linear descent killed at zero. Finally, we identify the joint limiting distribution of the unscaled pre-terminal position and terminal overshoot, including continuous and discontinuous termination.

We study the minimax regret rate for episodic kernel-based reinforcement learning, where the expected reward and transition density belong to a Sobolev reproducing kernel Hilbert space, with continuous state and action spaces, and adversarial initial states. For Sobolev smoothness parameter $
u>0$, state dimension $d_S$, and action dimension $d_A$, we prove that the minimax expected regret over $T$ episodes is $\widetilde\Theta(T^{\max\{e_A,e_B\}})$, where $e_A= rac{
u+d_A}{2
u+d_A}$, $e_B= rac{
u+d_A+3d_S/2}{2
u+d_A+2d_S}$ with the other model parameters fixed. The two exponents reflect the distinct difficulties of action selection and learning across states. We introduce Sobolev Optimal Value Iteration (SOVI), which attains this rate from observed rewards and transitions. For fixed smoothness and reference-kernel lengthscale, its regret bound has a prefactor polynomial in the state-action dimension $d=d_S+d_A$, horizon $H$, transition and reward RKHS norm bounds $u,B_r$, and kernel norm-comparison factor $\Lambda$, up to logarithmic factors. The algorithm separates initial action selection from continuation-value estimation and combines local polynomial approximation with the shared RKHS structure of the approximation errors. Our matching upper and lower bounds determine the optimal dependence on the number of episodes for Sobolev kernel-based reinforcement learning. Thus, we partially address the open problem in Vakili(2024) under the condition of the Sobolev kernel setup.
